  "description": "Discontinued, replaced by the current Solaris. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Solaris.\n\nThe SolarisMAX was our ultimate all-rounder hardtail: 29er wheels, smiles for miles. Confidence inspiring, agile and fun, planted at high speed on the rocks and a singletrack scalpel in the corners. It was the downcountry hardtail tool of choice, using our Longshot geometry for sweet, short stem handling, technical trail confidence and a roomy cockpit for long distance comfort.\n\nRun the minimum 120mm travel fork and the SolarisMAX stayed true to its roots: more than happy whizzing around 12 hour long distance races, scrambling up technical climbs, or off bikepacking in the wilderness. Go to 130 or 140mm if you occasionally want more speed or steeper tech. The Reynolds 853 frame has our famously subtle, traction-rich ride feel, with space for bags and bottles on long days. It could switch from a high precision trail centre warrior to a 2.6\" tyre, high-traction monster truck, a light and lively downcountry blade, a bikepacking rig or a map-crossing smoothie.\n\nFinishes: Supernova Orange, Froggatt Green, Midnight Blue and Hubble Purple (the 2022 batch). Earlier batches included Supernova Orange and Midnight Blue.",
